--- !u!114 &1191605238
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1191605235}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 17c4c63378daf1d48a91dd4bb1d2cb82, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DefenderOfIndependence.Level2.LevelTwoConversationTrigger
  activeDay: 1
  conversationDisplayName: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
  interactionCollider: {fileID: 1314323562}
  energyCost: 1
  cameraFocusTarget: {fileID: 511930727}
  calculateFinalResultOnComplete: 0
  steps:
  - lines:
    - speaker: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
      text: Before we face the British government, our own delegation must agree
        on what we are asking for.
    speaker: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
    prompt: Before we face the British government, our own delegation must agree
      on what we are asking for.
    choices:
    - text: 'We should agree on one clear objective: self-government leading to independence,
        while preparing answers on security and administration.'
      responseSpeaker: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
      response: Good. Independence is our objective, but a united delegation must
        also show that we understand the responsibilities that come with governing
        a country. We cannot arrive in London with only a demand; we must arrive
        with a plan.
      meterChange:
        britishConfidence: 5
        delegationUnity: 15
        publicSupport: 0
    - text: Demand immediate independence and refuse to discuss any British concerns.
      responseSpeaker: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
      response: Determination is important, but refusing every discussion would make
        the conference pointless. Some may applaud a stronger demand, yet we still
        need an agreement that can actually move Malaya toward independence.
      meterChange:
        britishConfidence: -15
        delegationUnity: -5
        publicSupport: 10
    - text: Let every delegate present a different position.
      responseSpeaker: TUNKU ABDUL RAHMAN
      response: Then we would appear divided before negotiations have even begun.
        We may disagree during preparation, but once we enter the conference we must
        understand what we are trying to achieve together.
      meterChange:
        britishConfidence: -5
        delegationUnity: -15
        publicSupport: 0
